<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wetwang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wetwang is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorkshire-wolds">Yorkshire Wolds</a> in the East Riding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorkshire">Yorkshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. Excavations at nearby Wetwang Slack revealed a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> cemetery of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arras-culture">Arras culture</a>, and in 2001 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> burial of a woman, dated to around 300 BCE, was found in the village during building work. These finds are among the richest evidence for the Iron Age people of East Yorkshire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wetwang.jpg" alt="Wetwang" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jonathan Thacker · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Nicholas_Church_Wetwang_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
